module

public import Degenne2023Existence.D2023.Setting

/-!
# Lemma 11 of [D23]: the large deviation principle of the empirical mean

The empirical mean of `n` independent samples of the member of mean `μ` of a one-parameter
canonical exponential family satisfies the large deviation principle with speed `n` and good rate
function `x ↦ KL(x, μ)`: Cramér's theorem for exponential families. The rate function is the
divergence `d(x, μ)` of the family at its means `x`, extended to every level by the Cramér rate
function of the member of mean `μ` (`Measure.expFamilyRate`).

## Main statements

* `Degenne2023Existence.isLDP_empiricalMean_expFamily`: [D23, Lemma 11].

## References

* [D23] R. Degenne, *On the existence of a complexity in fixed budget bandit identification*,
  COLT 2023, arXiv:2303.09468v2.
-/

@[expose] public section

open MeasureTheory LMLExplore

namespace Degenne2023Existence

/-- **Cramér's theorem for exponential families** [D23, Lemma 11]. For a mean `μ` of the
exponential family generated by `ρ` with the statistic `id`, the laws of the empirical means
`(∑ i < n, X i) / n` of `n` independent samples of the member of mean `μ` satisfy the large
deviation principle with speed `n` and good rate function `x ↦ KL(x, μ)`, the Cramér rate function
`ρ.expFamilyRate id x μ` of the member of mean `μ`. -/
theorem isLDP_empiricalMean_expFamily {ρ : Measure ℝ} {μ : ℝ} (hμ : μ ∈ ρ.expFamilyMeans id) :
    IsLDP (fun n ↦ (Measure.pi fun _ : Fin n ↦ ρ.expFamily id (ρ.natParam id μ)).map
        fun x : Fin n → ℝ ↦ (∑ i, x i) / (n : ℝ)) (fun x ↦ ρ.expFamilyRate id x μ) ∧
      IsGoodRateFunction (fun x ↦ ρ.expFamilyRate id x μ) := by
  sorry

end Degenne2023Existence
